1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:01,510
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:04,130
I built a system that takes a video idea,

3
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:06,300
plans and generates the shots,

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,271
reviews the results,

5
00:00:07,271 --> 00:00:10,260
and turns everything into a finished video.

6
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,080
For this demo, I'll quickly show you

7
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,770
the process and the final output.

8
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:17,320
The process starts with a simple request.

9
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,739
Instead of giving Conductor

10
00:00:18,739 --> 00:00:20,473
a long prompt every time,

11
00:00:20,473 --> 00:00:22,177
I moved the recurring instructions

12
00:00:22,177 --> 00:00:23,650
into the workflow.

13
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:25,910
Now I can give it a short request,

14
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:28,450
and the system handles the rest of the process.

15
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:31,260
The first thing the system does

16
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:33,890
is look at this existing video library.

17
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:35,877
This library gives the system examples

18
00:00:35,877 --> 00:00:37,610
of different video styles,

19
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:40,620
pacing, transitions, and storytelling.

20
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:43,108
It uses those references as inspiration

21
00:00:43,108 --> 00:00:44,600
to plan a new video,

22
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,130
rather than copying one directly.

23
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,010
After reviewing the references,

24
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,280
the system breaks the idea into individual shots.

25
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,243
For this video, it created four shots

26
00:00:54,243 --> 00:00:56,460
with their own purpose, timing,

27
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:58,570
copy, and visual direction.

28
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:00,593
Here, I'm showing three of them:

29
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:01,750
the initial brief,

30
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,220
the campaign idea,

31
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,528
and how that idea expands

32
00:01:04,528 --> 00:01:07,060
into different marketing assets.

33
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:09,570
For this project, the system chose HyperFrames

34
00:01:10,075 --> 00:01:11,220
because the video needed

35
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:13,940
precise text, UI, and layout

36
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,930
instead of generative footage.

37
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:18,028
For other videos, it can use models

38
00:01:18,028 --> 00:01:19,520
available through Fal

39
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,023
when the shot needs things like

40
00:01:21,023 --> 00:01:24,060
cinematic movement or generated footage.

41
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,962
The idea is to choose the method

42
00:01:25,962 --> 00:01:27,780
that best fits the shot,

43
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:29,067
instead of using the same model

44
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:30,660
for everything.

45
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,780
Once the individual shots are ready,

46
00:01:33,236 --> 00:01:35,120
they're combined into the final video.

47
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,875
The workflow then checks things like

48
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:39,680
timing, transitions, audio,

49
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,850
and the final output

50
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:43,350
before considering the video complete.

51
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:45,050
For every finished video,

52
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:46,483
the system creates its own

53
00:01:46,483 --> 00:01:48,550
reverse-engineering document.

54
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:50,580
This records how the video was made,

55
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,436
including the prompts, structure,

56
00:01:52,436 --> 00:01:54,139
methods used, revisions,

57
00:01:54,139 --> 00:01:55,280
and key learnings.

58
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,780
The workflow also checks

59
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:57,946
that this file exists

60
00:01:57,946 --> 00:02:00,560
before the video can be marked complete.

61
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,151
And this is the final video

62
00:02:02,151 --> 00:02:03,890
produced through that workflow.

63
00:02:40,987 --> 00:02:42,403
The next phase I'm working on

64
00:02:42,403 --> 00:02:44,047
is human realism,

65
00:02:44,047 --> 00:02:46,407
especially improving natural movement,

66
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:48,207
hands, eye direction,

67
00:02:48,207 --> 00:02:50,137
and longer scenes with people.

68
00:02:50,137 --> 00:02:52,612
I'm keeping that research separate for now

69
00:02:52,612 --> 00:02:55,067
while I continue testing and improving it.
